/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"subscribed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2021-03-24T13:02:28Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/805981472","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/8726#issuecomment-805981472","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/8726","id":805981472,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDgwNTk4MTQ3Mg==","user":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-03-24T16:41:42Z","updated_at":"2021-03-24T16:41:42Z","body":"I can reproduce the issue. It's caused by the view with ID `exo_controls_background` in `exo_styled_player_control_view.xml`, which uses `\"match_parent\"`, which is problematic if the view is included using `\"warp_content\"` in application code. I agree the current behaviour is strange, and let's use this issue to track fixing it.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure to what extent I think `android:layout_height=\"wrap_content\"` is a common use case. The problem with this approach is that until the video has loaded, the aspect ratio is not known. As a result, when sizing the player view in this way, you'll see its height change at the point where playback is prepared and the aspect ratio of the video becomes known. This change is unlikely to be a good user experience. I think a more common approach would be to set the height to a fixed value, which you could do in code using a calculation based on the available width and your desired aspect ratio. It's a tiny bit like how using `wrap_content` doesn't make sense for the scrolling direction of a scrolling view, although it's a lot less clear cut!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/805981472/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/806064892","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/8726#issuecomment-806064892","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/8726","id":806064892,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDgwNjA2NDg5Mg==","user":{"login":"Bradleycorn","id":4521694,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MjE2OTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4521694?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn","html_url":"https://github.com/Bradleycorn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-03-24T18:37:56Z","updated_at":"2021-03-24T18:37:56Z","body":"Thanks @ojw28 . My use case is similar to the demo project, with a few significant differences ... My containing Fragment view is a `MotionLayout`, and in its initial state the player isn't displayed at all (it's `gone`).  Then, upon some event (user clicks a button), we load a video stream and transition the `MotionLayout` to show the player. The stream that gets loaded can vary somewhat (though most are either 16:9 or 4:3), which precludes me from setting a fixed height. And while I can calculate the height easily enough, `MotionLayout` does not give me a way (that I know of) to set transition states dynamically at runtime.\r\n\r\nFWIW, I tried copying the `exo_styled_player_view.xml` and `exo_styled_player_control_view.xml` and making my own versions with wrap_content on the various elements to no avail.  ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/806064892/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"Bradleycorn","id":4521694,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MjE2OTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4521694?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn","html_url":"https://github.com/Bradleycorn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bradleycorn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":4503664955,"node_id":"MDE0Ok1lbnRpb25lZEV2ZW50NDUwMzY2NDk1NQ==","url":"https://ap